## Introduction

Artificial intelligence continues to evolve at a rapid pace, and agentic AI stands out as a significant leap forward. It introduces the concept of AI systems acting as autonomous agents, capable of making decisions and taking actions without constant human intervention. This shift has significant implications for businesses, individuals, and society as a whole. This report aims to provide a comprehensive understanding of agentic AI, covering its key aspects and potential impact.

_Links Used:_
*  https://hbr.org/2024/12/what-is-agentic-ai-and-how-will-it-change-work
* https://www.getmesa.com/blog/understanding-agentic-ai/



## Key Concepts

Agentic AI distinguishes itself from traditional AI through its ability to operate autonomously within defined boundaries. Key characteristics include goal-oriented behavior, proactive decision-making, adaptive learning, and the ability to interact with other agents and systems.  It's crucial to understand the distinction between agentic AI and AI agents, with the former focusing on comprehensive workflows and the latter representing individual components within those workflows.  Agentic AI emphasizes the orchestration of multiple AI agents and tools to achieve broader objectives.

